          "text": "A larger headline is one hierarchy cue, but not the only one. Weight, color, position, spacing, and alignment also shape what appears primary or secondary. Strong hierarchy uses a few coordinated differences. Random changes create noise; consistent differences create relationships that readers can learn quickly."
